{%- comment -%}
  Florista variant picker — one control per product option, for ANY product
  that has real options. The owner, 2026-09-07: "make it so i can do product
  varints for all itmes in the shop if i wish".

  What it replaces. The product page had no chooser at all. The form posted a
  hidden `id` pinned to the first available variant, and the only option UI in
  the whole theme was a hardcoded special case for digit balloons:

      {% if product.options contains 'כמה ספרות' %}

  Any other option name fell through that `if` and drew nothing, so adding a
  size in the admin created a variant no customer could reach. This snippet
  asks the general question — does this product have options — instead.

  Renders nothing at all when:
    · the product has only Shopify's default Title/"Default Title" option.
      Every single-variant product on the store is therefore byte-for-byte
      unchanged, which is all of them today except the balloons; or
    · it is a digit-balloon product. Those keep their age box: typing 67 is
      better than picking from a list of five, and florista-age-picker.js
      already owns the price there. Two scripts owning one number is how a
      stale price ships.

  Pills rather than a dropdown, decided on mobile first. Two or three sizes is
  the common case; a pill row shows every choice, and its availability, with
  no tap. Long value lists simply wrap.

  On the radio names: with no add-on ticked, florista-atc.js posts
  `new FormData(form)` straight to /cart/add.js, so every named field in this
  form is sent. `fp-option-*` cannot collide with `id`, `quantity`,
  `properties[…]` or `selling_plan`, so the cart API ignores it.

  No-JS: the radios are inert but the hidden `id` still holds a real, available
  variant, so the form degrades to exactly today's behaviour rather than
  breaking. The chosen variant is applied by JS only.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign fvp_show = true
  if product.has_only_default_variant
    assign fvp_show = false
  endif
  if product.options contains 'כמה ספרות'
    assign fvp_show = false
  endif
-%}

{%- if fvp_show -%}
  {%- capture fvp_variants -%}
    [
    {%- for v in product.variants -%}
      {
        "id": {{ v.id }},
        "options": {{ v.options | json }},
        "price": {{ v.price | json }},
        "priceText": {{ v.price | money | json }},
        {%- if v.compare_at_price and v.compare_at_price > v.price -%}
          "compareAtText": {{ v.compare_at_price | money | json }},
        {%- else -%}
          "compareAtText": null,
        {%- endif -%}
        "available": {{ v.available | json }},
        {%- comment -%} Per-variant photo, 2026-09-23: a colour option (the orchid in
            לבן / סגול / צהוב) is meaningless if the picture stays on the first colour.
            Same widths as the main <img> in florista-product.liquid, so the swapped
            srcset is the one the browser already sized for. Null when the variant has
            no image of its own; the JS then leaves the picture alone. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if v.featured_media -%}
          {%- assign fvp_widths = '375,550,750,1100,1400' | split: ',' -%}
          {%- capture fvp_srcset -%}
            {%- for w in fvp_widths -%}
              {%- assign wn = w | plus: 0 -%}
              {{ v.featured_media | image_url: width: wn }} {{ w }}w{%- unless forloop.last -%}, {%- endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endcapture -%}
          "image": { "src": {{ v.featured_media | image_url: width: 1400 | json }}, "srcset": {{ fvp_srcset | strip | json }}, "alt": {{ v.featured_media.alt | json }} }
        {%- else -%}
          "image": null
        {%- endif -%}
      }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    ]
  {%- endcapture -%}

  <div class="fp-variants" data-variant-picker data-variants="{{ fvp_variants | strip | escape }}">
    {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
      <fieldset class="fp-variant-group" data-option-index="{{ forloop.index0 }}">
        <legend class="fp-variant-legend">{{ option.name }}</legend>
        <div class="fp-variant-values">
          {%- for value in option.values -%}
            {%- assign fvp_id = 'fp-opt-' | append: section.id | append: '-' | append: forloop.parentloop.index | append: '-' | append: forloop.index -%}
            <input
              class="fp-variant-radio visually-hidden"
              type="radio"
              id="{{ fvp_id }}"
              name="fp-option-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.parentloop.index }}"
              value="{{ value | escape }}"
              {% if option.selected_value == value %}checked{% endif %}
            >
            <label class="fp-variant-pill" for="{{ fvp_id }}">{{ value }}</label>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      </fieldset>
    {%- endfor -%}
    <p class="fp-variant-sold-out" data-variant-soldout hidden>הצירוף הזה אזל מהמלאי</p>
  </div>

  <script src="{{ 'florista-variant-picker.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}
